#: ../../media.rst:3
msgid "Images, video, audio, and downloads"
msgstr "Imágenes, vídeo, audio y descargas"

#: ../../media.rst:6
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Keep a resource near the document that explains it. Name it with a "
#| "relative path, or start the path with ``/`` to refer to the source "
#| "root. Guidedog copies resources used by the documents. A video remains "
#| "a video on the web; a PDF names the recording."
msgid ""
"We keep a resource near the document that explains it. We name it with a "
"relative path, or start the path with ``/`` to refer to the source root. "
"Guidedog copies the resources that the documents use. A video remains a "
"video on the web. A PDF names the recording."
msgstr ""
"Mantenga los recursos cerca del documento que los explica. Use rutas "
"relativas o empiece por ``/`` para referirse a la raíz de fuentes. "
"Guidedog copia los recursos usados. El vídeo sigue siendo vídeo en la "
"web; el PDF identifica la grabación."

#: ../../media.rst:10
msgid "Images"
msgstr "Imágenes"

#: ../../media.rst:23
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Pages copy images into ``_images``; the book embeds them. PNG, JPEG, "
#| "GIF, SVG, and WebP work in both. A missing image is a warning: the "
#| "page keeps the image's alternative text, and the book leaves the image "
#| "out."
msgid ""
"Pages copy images into ``_images``. The book embeds them. PNG, JPEG, GIF, "
"SVG, and WebP work in both. A missing image is a warning: the page keeps "
"the image's alternative text, and the book leaves the image out."
msgstr ""
"Las páginas copian las imágenes en ``_images``\\ ; el libro las incrusta. "
"PNG, JPEG, GIF, SVG y WebP funcionan en ambos. Una imagen ausente genera "
"una advertencia: la página conserva el texto alternativo y el libro omite "
"la imagen."

#: ../../media.rst:27
msgid "Video and audio"
msgstr "Vídeo y audio"

#: ../../media.rst:30
msgid ""
"An image or figure that names a video (``.mp4``, ``.webm``, ``.ogv``, "
"``.mov``, ``.m4v``) or an audio file (``.mp3``, ``.ogg``, ``.oga``, "
"``.m4a``, ``.opus``, ``.wav``, ``.flac``, ``.aac``) plays it, as Docutils "
"does for video:"
msgstr ""
"Una imagen o figura que apunta a vídeo (\\ ``.mp4``\\ , ``.webm``\\ , "
"``.ogv``\\ , ``.mov``\\ , ``.m4v``\\ ) o audio (\\ ``.mp3``\\ , "
"``.ogg``\\ , ``.oga``\\ , ``.m4a``\\ , ``.opus``\\ , ``.wav``\\ , "
"``.flac``\\ , ``.aac``\\ ) lo reproduce, como hace Docutils con el vídeo:"

#: ../../media.rst:44
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Pages show the browser's player, with a link to the file for browsers "
#| "that cannot play it. A book cannot play media, so it names the "
#| "recording in a box where the player would be; text output writes "
#| "``[video: ...]`` or ``[audio: ...]``."
msgid ""
"Pages show the browser's player, with a link to the file for browsers "
"that cannot play it. A book cannot play media, so it names the recording "
"in a box where the player would be. Text output writes ``[video: ...]`` "
"or ``[audio: ...]``."
msgstr ""
"Las páginas muestran el reproductor del navegador y un enlace al archivo "
"por si no puede reproducirse. Un libro no reproduce multimedia, por lo "
"que identifica la grabación en un recuadro. La salida de texto escribe "
"``[video: ...]`` o ``[audio: ...]``\\ ."

#: ../../media.rst:48
msgid "Downloads"
msgstr "Descargas"

#: ../../media.rst:51
msgid ""
"In HTML, the ``download`` role copies a file into ``_downloads`` and "
"offers it for saving:"
msgstr ""
"En HTML, el rol ``download`` copia el archivo en ``_downloads`` y ofrece "
"guardarlo:"

#: ../../media.rst:58
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "For portable PDF download links, set ``html_baseurl`` to the published "
#| "HTML site's absolute HTTP or HTTPS address. The book then links to "
#| "that site's copied files. Without it, the link remains "
#| "source-relative; the PDF does not embed attachments. This setting does "
#| "not upload files. Publish the HTML site before sharing the book. This "
#| "behavior is available in Guidedog 0.6.3 and later."
msgid ""
"For portable PDF download links, set ``html_baseurl`` to the published "
"HTML site's absolute HTTP or HTTPS address. The book then links to that "
"site's copied files. Without it, the link remains source-relative. The "
"PDF does not embed attachments. This setting does not upload files. "
"Publish the HTML site before sharing the book. This behavior is available "
"in Guidedog 0.6.3 and later."
msgstr ""
"Para que los enlaces funcionen en un PDF independiente, defina "
"``html_baseurl`` con la dirección HTTP o HTTPS absoluta del sitio "
"publicado. El libro enlazará a los archivos copiados allí. Sin ella, las "
"rutas siguen siendo relativas a las fuentes; el PDF no incorpora "
"adjuntos. Esta opción no sube archivos: publique el sitio HTML antes de "
"compartir el libro. Este comportamiento está disponible en Guidedog 0.6.3 "
"y versiones posteriores."

#: ../../media.rst:64
msgid "Theme files"
msgstr "Archivos del tema"

#: ../../media.rst:67
msgid ""
"``_static`` holds the files the theme uses (style sheets, scripts, fonts, "
"a logo), copied as they are into ``_static`` in the site. "
"``html_static_path`` lists it, and ``html_css_files``, ``html_js_files``, "
"``html_logo``, and ``html_favicon`` name files in it. Content media "
"belongs with the documents instead, so that moving a document with its "
"media keeps its links working."
msgstr ""
"``_static`` contiene hojas de estilo, scripts, fuentes y logotipos del "
"tema, que se copian sin cambios a ``_static`` del sitio. "
"``html_static_path`` indica la carpeta; ``html_css_files``\\ , "
"``html_js_files``\\ , ``html_logo`` y ``html_favicon`` nombran sus "
"archivos. El contenido multimedia debe ir junto a los documentos para "
"conservar los enlaces al moverlos."

